Upstream: https://github.com/vim/vim/commit/bdcb63d47fa5e86406a7b04a0ab62638018fb6b5
GHSA-26qr-jvfj-hcwm (Low; a CVE is requested, none assigned), patch 9.2.1309: a spell
file with two SN_SOFO sections freed the first one's items as SN_SAL items, reading past
the allocation; a modeline that sets 'spelllang' to a .spl path loads one by opening a
file. A second soundfold section (SAL or SOFO) is now a format error. Upstream's commit
as it is, but for its test and version.c; spellfile.c applies to 9.2.1250 unchanged.
Not a pin of 9.2.1309: every tag from 9.2.1255 on has runtime/syntax/shared/
debversions.vim run debian-distro-info and ubuntu-distro-info, a new process this fix
does not need (R57), which waits for Joshua.
Drop this when pkg:vim moves to 9.2.1309 or later.

From bdcb63d47fa5e86406a7b04a0ab62638018fb6b5 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Christian Brabandt <cb@256bit.org>
Date: Sun, 8 Nov 2026 21:44:18 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] patch 9.2.1309:[security]: heap-buffer-overflow with two SOFO
 sections

Problem:  [security]: A spell file with two SN_SOFO sections frees the
          first one's items as SN_SAL items, reading beyond the
          allocated memory (pangflame).
Solution: Give a format error when more than one section is found.

Github Security Advisory:
https://github.com/vim/vim/security/advisories/GHSA-26qr-jvfj-hcwm

Assisted-by: Claude
Signed-off-by: Christian Brabandt <cb@256bit.org>
---
 src/spellfile.c | 13 +++++++++----
 1 file changed, 9 insertions(+), 4 deletions(-)

diff --git a/src/spellfile.c b/src/spellfile.c
index a2853f5..15ed18b 100644
--- a/src/spellfile.c
+++ b/src/spellfile.c
@@ -353,6 +353,7 @@ spell_load_file(
     int		c = 0;
     int		res;
     int		did_estack_push = FALSE;
+    bool	had_soundfold = false;
     ESTACK_CHECK_DECLARATION;

     fd = mch_fopen((char *)fname, "r");
@@ -470,11 +471,15 @@ spell_load_file(
 		break;

 	    case SN_SAL:
-		res = read_sal_section(fd, lp);
-		break;
-
 	    case SN_SOFO:
-		res = read_sofo_section(fd, lp);
+		// there should either be a SN_SAL or SN_SOFO section
+		if (had_soundfold)
+		    res = SP_FORMERROR;
+		else if (n == SN_SAL)
+		    res = read_sal_section(fd, lp);
+		else
+		    res = read_sofo_section(fd, lp);
+		had_soundfold = true;
 		break;

 	    case SN_MAP:
--
